<title>USA: ADM says cutting back soybean crush pace.</title>
<headline>ADM says cutting back soybean crush pace.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Archer Daniels Midland Co is cutting back its soybean crushing operations in response to falling crush margins and limited soybean availability, company spokeswoman Karla Miller said.</p>
<p>&quot;The answer is yes,&quot; Miller said, when asked if low soybean supplies and weakening margins caused the company to slow crushing operations. Talk was circulating in cash markets on Friday that ADM was cutting back the crush pace at its plants across the U.S.</p>
<p>Miller declined, however, to give details of how much, when or at which locations the company was cutting back its soybean crush.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
